{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1523407-instability-in-other-splats","id":1523407,"title":"Instability in other splats?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Deviant: The Renegades"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-10-01T07:15:21-07:00","id":1523407,"title":"Instability in other splats?","content":"Deviant Devoted Companion page 15 has the new variation Absorb Instability, which at \u2022\u2022+ has the ability to transfer instability from the target to the user. Given that Sacred Flesh on page 151 of Deviant the Renegades allows for the Deviant to pass a Variation to a Baseline or one of the other splats, how do you think you (or your Storyteller) would adjudicate Instability on non-Remade?<br /> <br /> P.S. I know that page 151 of Deviant the Renegades states: &quot;The character who gains the secondary Variation has full command of it, exactly as though she were a Deviant wielding it, and it lasts until the end of the scene. A Baseline who is unprepared for this power may suffer a breaking point (p. 187) or may cause unintended harm because he is unfamiliar with his new capabilities.&quot;, which gives the ST an easy way to say that attempting Absorb Instability is too much of a breaking point for all the other splats and they could never willing or unwillingly activate the variation ... but the spirit of the question is what would happen if we &quot;Yes, And&quot; / &quot;Yes, But&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28213-raw_brewer_devoted","name":"RAW_brewer_devoted","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28213_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-01T08:41:21-07:00","id":1523421,"title":"","content":"As a loose one-size-fits-all approach: Take cues from the Forceful effect of Telepathy, inflicting a breaking point on Baseline users (applying penalties to the roll for Instabilities above minor and rolling for each Instability transferred) and draining Willpower from other monsters (doubling and tripling the drain for medium and major Instabilities and not allowing more Instability to be transferred than you can pay for).<br /> <br /> For slightly more effort, you could apply scaling Persistent Conditions that exacerbate or introduce the monster's normal types of issues \u2014 penalizing frenzy rolls or applying new banes (and lowering effective Humanity for existing ones) for vampires, shifting effective Harmony out of whack and applying Bans for werewolves, lowering effective Wisdom for the purposes of Paradox and the Long-Term Nimbus and applying or intensifying Paradox Conditions for mages, raising effective Azoth for the purposes of Disquiet/Torment/Wastelands for Prometheans, adding dice to Clarity damage rolls and intensifying or adding frailties to changelings, penalizing Intercession rolls and strengthening the Liminal Aura for Sin-Eaters, raising effective Sekhem for the purposes of Sybaris and the Descent timer for mummies, penalizing compromise rolls and raising effective Primum for glitch acquisition for demons, and adjusting effective Lair and Satiety for feeding/hunger purposes and messing with Anathema for Beasts, to rattle off a quick set of examples. If a splat has a failstate analogous to the Remade condition (e.g. Zi'ir, Enraptured, wild entitlements), taking in Instability should move them closer to it and/or replicate some of its effects.<br /> <br /> That being said, the particular combination of &quot;I can give other characters the means of absorbing Instability from Deviants at will but cannot do so myself without putting in a filler dot of Magnitude&quot; feels like the kind of potential ouroboros interaction for which the sidebar about not every possible combination of Variation/Scar/Deviation effect makes sense and the book can't possibly account for all of them; if I wanted to model a lendable ability to siphon off Instability I'd do so as a conspiracy Icon instead of something readily reproducible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-01T09:57:30-07:00","id":1523427,"title":"","content":"<b>Mortal (including hunters):</b> Take any instability as aggravated damage.<br /> <b>Vampire, Werewolf, Promethean:</b> Take a minor instability as lethal damage, a medium instability as two points of lethal damage, and a major instability as aggravated damage.<br /> <b>Mage:</b> Treat a minor or medium instability as an added Reach on the mage's next spell, with the medium instability also applying a +1 modifier to the mage's next Paradox roll. Suffer a major instability as a Paradox Condition with successes equal to the deviant's highest Variation Magnitude.<br /> <b>Changeling:</b> Take a minor instability as mild Clarity damage, a medium instability as severe Clarity damage, and a major instability as both severe Clarity damage and a Clarity Condition.<br /> <b>Geist:</b> Step your geist's trigger down from specific to vague or from vague to hazy. If your trigger is already hazy, suffer the effects of the Wavering Condition. These effects end after a number of crisis points equal to instabilities absorbed. A medium instability steps your trigger down a second time, or if already hazy, prevents intercession for one crisis point. If you absorb a major instability, die.<br /> <b>Mummy: </b>Make a Descent roll for each instability absorbed. Minor instabilities subtract three dice from the roll. If you absorb a major instability, die.<br /> <b>Demon:</b> Suffer each instability as a transient glitch: minor instability as minor glitch, medium as major, and major as catastrophic.<br /> <b>Beast:</b> Your Satiety falls once for each instability absorbed. The first medium instability absorbed inflicts the Soul Shocked Condition, and the first major instability inflicts an Anathema. Medium or major instabilities past this drop Satiety twice each.<br /> <br /> With the Resilient effect of Absorb Instability, instead of healing or downgrading an instability herself, the target heals or downgrades the instability that would have been transferred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-01T17:27:08-07:00","id":1523444,"title":"","content":"Thanks!<br /> <br /> Honestly the best I had come up with so far was to give the Baseline/splat an Instability tracker of 5 + their Supernatural Tolerance with the effects triggering based off of 5 rightmost boxes of the tracker triggering effects as per Deviant the Renegades page 87 ... but stapling an additional tracker onto Baselines/splats felt wrong.<br /> <br /> Definitely need to have an in depth conversation with ST before allowing a Sacred Flesh + Absorb Instability Variation (or an Agent Icon with the Absorb Instability Variation (with or without the commensurate Scar) as per page 26 of The Devoted Companion), but I definitely feel a lot more confident about running it if a player tries it out (or if the cohort decides the conspiracy would experiment with Instability).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28213-raw_brewer_devoted","name":"RAW_brewer_devoted","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28213_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}